\section*{The Dirac-Brown invariant-subspace problem: a defect-attainment reduction}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
At every fixed irrational rotation angle, a continuous nonnegative weight with one zero and divergent negative logarithmic integral is claimed to produce a nonzero quasinilpotent operator without factor-invariant projections. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 293, 2026-09-27): Rare, increasingly deep drops define a measurable model whose invariance equations cannot reconcile a surviving central convolution coefficient with a suppressed infinite tail. Mixed-radix couplings control the orbit-pair tests at the prescribed angle. Smoothing the drops changes their logarithms by a measurable coboundary; an affiliated intertwiner transfers any invariant projection, preserving trace and hence the obstruction.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Manuscript 1 (family 293, 2026-09-27): The main theorem constructs in the hyperfinite II1 factor a bounded operator with Brown measure delta\_0 and no nonzero proper affiliated invariant projection, exactly refuting this problem’s universal Dirac-Brown assertion.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For family 293, the scope page documents the following selections. The rotation selection gives quasinilpotent weighted operators with no proper invariant projection in the associated finite factor. The backward-intertwiner selection gives a proper strong-closed transitive commutant on each separable infinite-dimensional Hilbert space; Brown-measure and product variants are documented separately. The documented statement covers the main claim of manuscript 1. Its selected declaration also covers the clause used for this problem. Comparator files: BackwardIntertwiners.lean, ContinuousCircleWeight.lean, FiniteFactor.lean, HyperinvariantSubspaces.lean, IrrationalRotation.lean, ProductBrown.lean. Declarations: OAI.BackwardIntertwiners.direct\_algebra\_corollary, OAI.ContinuousCircleWeight.main\_theorem, OAI.FiniteFactor.main\_theorem, OAI.Hyperinvariant.main\_theorem, OAI.Invariant233.Results.prescribed\_irrational\_counterexample, OAI.Invariant233.Results.product\_realization, OAI.FiniteFactor.productBrown.

This site has not executed the Lean files or checked their dependencies. These descriptions report the scope of the linked declarations, rather than a new verification of the proofs.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these results to an internal model. Its release notice cautions that results lacking full formalization can contain mistakes. This site has not independently assessed the proofs; a solved label records the scope of the reported claim.

